 # Materials
 
-Phase 1 now includes the baseline isotropic material family required by later grid,
-compiler, boundary, and source work.
+Phase 1 now includes the baseline isotropic material family plus the first general
+electric-dispersive medium path required by later compiler and runtime work.
 
 ## Supported Types
 
@@ -9,10 +9,12 @@
   `conductivity`, `permeability`, and `magnetic_conductivity`
 - `PECMedium`: perfect electric conductor marker
 - `PMCMedium`: perfect magnetic conductor marker
+- `PoleResidue`: homogeneous electric-dispersive medium with `eps_inf` plus explicit
+  complex-valued pole-residue pairs stored as JSON-safe `(real, imag)` tuples
 
 These models live in `autofdtd.materials`, are re-exported from `autofdtd.api`, and
-lower into typed execution IR (`MediumIR`, `PECMediumIR`, `PMCMediumIR`) rather than
