phase1/runs/task-022-attempt-001/result.json:1:{"task_id":"task-022","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented `StablePML` and `Absorber` boundary support across the public API, typed IR, boundary compiler, staged runtime path, examples, docs, and representative absorption tests.","key_findings":["`StablePML` and `Absorber` are now first-class public boundary edges with Tidy3D-aligned defaults, explicit `Boundary` / `BoundarySpec` constructors, and zero-dimension coercion behavior shared with baseline `PML`.","Boundary IR now distinguishes `PML`, `StablePML`, and `Absorber` through typed payloads (`PMLIR`, `StablePMLIR`, `AbsorberIR`) plus family-specific axis and face metadata on `BoundarySpecIR`.","Runtime compilation keeps the existing staged damping-layer seam: `StablePML` lowers onto the baseline PML coefficient path with a separate profile tag, while `Absorber` lowers into conductivity-only attenuation coefficients with a reflective outer-wall policy.","The absorbing-boundary runtime and state allocator now handle all three absorbing families through the shared staged kernel path, while kernel metadata advertises explicit `stable_pml` and `absorber` mode support.","Focused verification passed with `PYTHONPATH=src pytest -q tests/test_boundaries.py tests/test_ir.py tests/test_imports.py tests/test_containers.py` and `PYTHONPATH=src python -m compileall src/autofdtd`."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/boundaries/models.py","description":"Added `AbsorberParams`, `StablePML`, `Absorber`, and public constructors for the new absorbing boundary families."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/compiler/boundaries.py","description":"Extended absorbing-boundary compilation to prepare StablePML and Absorber coefficient profiles and per-family face metadata."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/kernels/boundaries.py","description":"Extended staged boundary kernels to handle StablePML and Absorber runtime modes."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/runtime/boundaries.py","description":"Updated runtime state allocation so all absorbing families share the staged boundary execution path."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Added typed IR lowering for `StablePML`, `Absorber`, and `AbsorberParams`."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_boundaries.py","description":"Added representative tests for StablePML and Absorber compilation, IR lowering, state allocation, reflective ghost behavior, and staged absorption."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/boundaries.md","description":"Updated boundary-scope documentation to cover the implemented absorbing-boundary subset and current limits."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-022-attempt-001/result.json","description":"Structured task result for this loop iteration."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"The current `StablePML` implementation is a preset-driven extension of the staged PML backend, and `Absorber` is a conductivity-ramp subset with a reflective outer wall. `task-023` should build ABC-family behavior on the existing absorbing-face metadata without redesigning the shared staged boundary seam.","next_action":"none"}
