phase1/runs/task-001-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:465:## [QUEUED] task-019 - Implement boundary support for Periodic, PECBoundary, PMCBoundary, and Boundary containers
phase1/runs/task-001-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:466:Success: Support the foundational non-absorbing boundary surface, including Boundary and BoundarySpec composition, periodic behavior, conductor boundaries, and the runtime transform or kernel support needed by the timestep loop.
phase1/runs/task-001-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:471:Notes: These are the first boundary primitives the compiler and runtime should rely on.
phase1/runs/task-001-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:481:## [QUEUED] task-021 - Implement PML boundary support with coefficient prep and kernel stages
phase1/runs/task-001-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:482:Success: Support PML boundaries with explicit API and IR models, coefficient preparation, boundary-layer state allocation, kernel-stage integration, and representative absorption tests.
phase1/runs/task-001-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:487:Notes: PML is important enough to deserve its own task instead of sharing a generic absorbing-boundary bucket.
phase1/runs/task-001-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:489:## [QUEUED] task-022 - Implement StablePML and Absorber boundary support with coefficient prep and kernel stages
