phase1/runs/task-012-attempt-001/result.json:1:{"task_id":"task-012","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented the Phase 1 subpixel policy surface with explicit `SubpixelSpec`, typed averaging and staircasing models, Tidy3D-style boolean coercion, and typed IR metadata for later geometry materialization.","key_findings":["`src/autofdtd/grid/subpixel.py` now models `SubpixelSpec`, `Staircasing`, and `PolarizedAveraging`, and normalizes `Simulation.subpixel` from either a bool or a tagged `SubpixelSpec` payload.","Phase 1 subpixel scope is explicit: dielectric interfaces can request `PolarizedAveraging`, while metal, PEC, PMC, and lossy-metal buckets remain staircasing-only until later anisotropic and conformal work lands.","`src/autofdtd/ir/models.py` now lowers subpixel settings into `SubpixelSpecIR` with per-family policies, `averaging_targets`, `staircasing_targets`, and `requires_anisotropic_materialization` for compiler handoff.","Validation now rejects deferred subpixel policy tags such as `ContourPathAveraging` with clear Phase 1 errors instead of accepting opaque dict payloads.","Verification passed for `pytest` over the Phase 1 test set, `ruff check src tests`, and targeted `mypy` on the new subpixel and IR modules."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/grid/subpixel.py","description":"Public Phase 1 subpixel policy models and normalization helpers."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/core/validation.py","description":"Validation hooks that normalize `Simulation.subpixel` and reject unsupported subpixel payloads clearly."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Typed `SubpixelSpecIR` lowering that exposes averaging targets and anisotropic-materialization requirements."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_grid.py","description":"Grid and subpixel tests covering defaults, staircasing fallback, and deferred-policy rejection."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_containers.py","description":"Simulation-level normalization tests for bool and explicit subpixel configurations."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_ir.py","description":"IR tests verifying typed subpixel lowering inside the simulation execution snapshot."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/examples/subpixel.py","description":"Example simulation using explicit Phase 1 subpixel controls."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/architecture.md","description":"Architecture notes updated to describe the new subpixel-policy seam and its Phase 1 scope."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/working-memory.md","description":"Condensed handoff notes capturing the subpixel-policy decisions for later compiler and material tasks."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/loop.spec.md","description":"Task board updated to mark `task-012` completed."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-012-attempt-001/result.json","description":"Recorded task output matching the Phase 1 result schema."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"`task-017` and later compiler/materialization work should treat `SubpixelSpecIR` as the source of truth for which interface families need tensor-valued effective media, while deferred conformal and volumetric policies remain explicit validation errors until their kernel and material support lands.","next_action":"none"}
