cation passed with `ruff check src tests`, `pytest -q tests/test_materials.py`, and `python -m compileall src`. A repo-wide `mypy src` run still reports pre-existing unrelated typing issues outside this task\u2019s scope.", "key_findings": ["`autofdtd.materials` now exposes `Lorentz`, `Drude`, and `Debye` models with analytical `eps_model()` evaluation, family-specific validation, and lowering to equivalent `PoleResidue` payloads.", "`autofdtd.ir` now emits typed `LorentzIR`, `DrudeIR`, and `DebyeIR` payloads, and the compiler preserves the originating family tag while compiling onto the existing `PoleResidueMaterialCoefficients` auxiliary-state contract.", "Compilation now fails explicitly when converted dispersive poles are too stiff for the current exact-hold timestep path, which clearly delimits the currently supported subset instead of emitting unusable coefficients.", "Examples, docs, tests, and working memory were updated so the new families are exercised and the subset boundary is recorded for later material/runtime tasks."], "message": "Implemented passive homogeneous Lorentz, damped Drude, and passive homogeneous Debye medium support across the public API, typed IR, coefficient compilation, and the shared PoleResidue-family update path, with explicit tests for each family.", "next_action": "none", "paths": {"codex_stdout": "/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-016-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt", "result_json": "/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-016-attempt-001/result.json", "run_dir": "/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-016-attempt-001"}, "result_status": "completed", "run_id": "task-016-attempt-001", "status": "COMPLETED", "task_id": "task-016", "task_title": "Implement Lorentz, Drude, and Debye medium support with update kernels", "tasks_remaining": 43, "ts": "2026-04-06T03:59:50Z"}
