phase1/runs/task-023-attempt-001/result.json:1:{"task_id":"task-023","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented a practical Phase 1 `ABCBoundary` subset with typed API/IR/compiler/runtime support, while making `ModeABCBoundary` and related mode-fit surfaces parseable but explicitly deferred.","key_findings":["`ABCBoundary` is now part of the implemented public boundary surface and compiles into explicit first-order recurrence coefficients plus persistent per-face ABC state for staged ghost updates.","Boundary runtime and IR metadata now expose `abc_axes` and `abc_faces`, keeping the mathematical boundary family distinct from scheduling and later chunk-planning concerns.","`ModeABCBoundary`, `BroadbandModeABCSpec`, and `BroadbandModeABCFitterParam` are now mapped compatibility surfaces, but Simulation validation and runtime compilation fail clearly because mode-solver dependencies are not available in Phase 1.","Docs, examples, tests, working memory, and the task result artifact were updated to capture the implemented ABC subset and the explicit defer policy for mode-based ABC."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/boundaries/models.py","description":"Public boundary models now include `ABCBoundary`, deferred `ModeABCBoundary` compatibility types, and convenience constructors on `Boundary` and `BoundarySpec`."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/compiler/boundaries.py","description":"Boundary compilation now prepares first-order ABC coefficients, `abc_*` face metadata, and explicit deferred errors for mode-based ABC."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/kernels/boundaries.py","description":"Boundary kernels now provide persistent ABC state models and staged electric/magnetic ABC ghost updates."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/runtime/boundaries.py","description":"Runtime orchestration now allocates ABC state alongside PML state and applies both staged boundary families."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"IR lowering now emits typed `ABCBoundaryIR` payloads and `BoundarySpecIR` `abc_axes` / `abc_faces` metadata."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_boundaries.py","description":"Focused tests cover ABC normalization, compilation, staged updates, IR lowering, and the explicit `ModeABCBoundary` defer behavior."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/boundaries.md","description":"Boundary documentation now explains the implemented ABC subset and the remaining `ModeABCBoundary` defer policy."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/runs/task-023-attempt-001/result.json","description":"Structured task result matching the Phase 1 output schema."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"Automatic boundary-medium inference for `ABCBoundary` and all mode-based ABC behavior should build on the new `abc_faces` staged-boundary seam once scene-material sampling and mode-solver tasks land.","next_action":"none"}
