phase1/runs/task-017-attempt-011/codex.stdout.txt:147:- `src/autofdtd/materials/dispersive.py` now provides a Phase 1 `PoleResidue` public model with JSON-safe complex-pair storage, causal validation (`Re(a) <= 0`), `eps_model()`, and limited `Medium` conversion helpers.
phase1/runs/task-017-attempt-011/codex.stdout.txt:151:- `src/autofdtd/ir/models.py` now lowers `Sellmeier` into a typed `SellmeierIR` while keeping runtime compilation on the shared pole-residue auxiliary-state contract.
phase1/runs/task-017-attempt-011/codex.stdout.txt:152:- `src/autofdtd/ir/models.py` now lowers `Lorentz`, `Drude`, and `Debye` into typed IR families while runtime compilation still targets the shared pole-residue auxiliary-state contract.
phase1/runs/task-017-attempt-011/codex.stdout.txt:155:- `src/autofdtd/compiler/materials.py` now compiles `Lorentz`, `Drude`, and `Debye` by first reducing them to equivalent `PoleResidue` terms, re-tagging the compiled coefficients with the public family name, and failing explicitly when converted poles are too stiff for the current exact-hold timestep path.
phase1/runs/task-017-attempt-011/codex.stdout.txt:160:- Reserve subsystem namespaces now: `api`, `core`, `geometry`, `materials`, `boundaries`, `sources`, `monitors`, `grid`, `modes`, `ir`, `compiler`, `runtime`, `kernels`, `diagnostics`, `examples`.
