phase1/logs/console.log:325555:phase1/logs/console.log:286184:phase1/runs/task-019-attempt-001/codex.stdout.txt:101129:+{"task_id":"task-019","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented the foundational non-absorbing boundary surface across the public API, typed IR, boundary compiler, ghost-update kernels, runtime wrapper, docs, and tests.","key_findings":["`autofdtd.boundaries` now exposes typed `Periodic`, `PECBoundary`, `PMCBoundary`, `Boundary`, and `BoundarySpec` models, including periodic-opposite-conductor coercion so one axis never mixes periodic and reflective runtime semantics.","`autofdtd.ir` now lowers the supported subset into typed `PeriodicIR`, `PECBoundaryIR`, `PMCBoundaryIR`, `BoundaryIR`, and `BoundarySpecIR` payloads while unsupported boundary families still fall back to the generic boundary envelope.","`autofdtd.compiler.boundaries.compile_boundary_spec()` now produces explicit per-face halo metadata, parity-sign transforms, periodic-versus-reflective axis grouping, and stage ordering for later timestep integration.","`autofdtd.kernels.boundaries` and `autofdtd.runtime.boundaries` now provide concrete ghost-cell update helpers for `(nx, ny, nz, 3)` vector fields, covering periodic copy behavior plus PEC and PMC reflection parity.","Examples, docs, working memory, and focused tests now exercise the public models, IR lowering, runtime compilation, explicit unsupported-boundary errors, and ghost-update behavior."],"artifacts":[{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/boundaries/models.py","description":"Added the typed non-absorbing boundary public models and normalization helpers."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/core/validation.py","description":"Extended normalization and zero-dimension coercion to understand the supported boundary subset."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/ir/models.py","description":"Added typed boundary IR classes and lowering helpers for the supported subset."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/compiler/boundaries.py","description":"Added boundary runtime compilation metadata for periodic, PEC, and PMC halo handling."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/kernels/boundaries.py","description":"Added concrete ghost-cell update helpers and boundary kernel metadata."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/runtime/boundaries.py","description":"Added the runtime wrapper that applies compiled boundary ghost updates."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/src/autofdtd/examples/boundaries.py","description":"Added a simple compiled-boundary example snapshot."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/docs/boundaries.md","description":"Documented the implemented subset, runtime lowering, and current limits."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/tests/test_boundaries.py","description":"Added focused tests for boundary normalization, IR lowering, compiler/runtime behavior, and explicit unsupported-boundary errors."},{"path":"/workspace/autofdtd/phase1/working-memory.md","description":"Recorded the boundary-runtime design decisions and handoff notes for later Bloch and absorber tasks."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"Verification passed with `PYTHONPATH=src pytest -q tests/test_boundaries.py tests/test_containers.py tests/test_ir.py`, `PYTHONPATH=src pytest -q tests/test_imports.py tests/test_planning.py`, and `PYTHONPATH=src python -m compileall src`. `ruff` was not installed in the environment, so lint verification could not be run here.","next_action":"none"}
